+## P0
+
+None.
+
+## P1
+
+1. **A cross-tab text-size change can reflow the article without preserving the reader’s place.** The proposed `resize` event makes `useRootFontPx()` update ([measure.ts:154](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/reader/measure.ts:154)), but the reflow key omits the root size ([Reader.tsx:718](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:718)). At widths where fitted column widths remain unchanged, every paragraph can rewrap while `layoutKey` does not change. Scroll restoration explicitly treats an unchanged key as “nothing reflowed” ([useReadingPosition.ts:155](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/reader/useReadingPosition.ts:155)), and the position spy has the same dependency ([useReadingPosition.ts:185](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/reader/useReadingPosition.ts:185)). Add `rootFontPx` or the text-size value to `layoutKey`, with a regression test where root size changes but `tableW`/`modeW` do not.
+
+2. **The plan’s preserved-contrast claim is false.** It says the overlay keeps text/page contrast at the same ratio ([plan:121](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/docs/plans/261019g-reading-comfort-on-profile-brightness-and-text-size.md:121)). Alpha compositing scales encoded RGB values, while WCAG contrast uses linear luminance plus a `0.05` term; the ratio therefore falls, often sharply. This matters because several muted colours were calibrated just above 4.5:1 ([tokens.css:182](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/styles/tokens.css:182)). Keep the overlay design, but describe it honestly and calibrate the three levels for readable body, muted, disabled, and danger text in both themes. Pixel brightness alone is insufficient acceptance evidence.
+
+3. **The claim that JS layout “gives up columns sooner” is only partly true, and the browser matrix misses the risky boundaries.** Standard bands retain fixed `MODE_MIN`/`MODE_IDEAL` values ([layout.ts:232](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/layout.ts:232)), fixed prose thresholds ([layout.ts:59](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/layout.ts:59), [layout.ts:125](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/layout.ts:125)), and the same 700px cover crossover ([layout.ts:482](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/layout.ts:482)). Marginalia remains 200/288/384px while its text grows ([layout.ts:529](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/layout.ts:529)). At a 22px root, the 400px prose floor is substantially narrower in characters than the 30.2ch measured at 16px. Either scale the type-readability thresholds or explicitly accept that trade-off and test 700px, the band-plus-marginalia crossover, narrow landscape, and a dense mode—not only 390px and 820px Plain/Glossary.
+
+4. **Dimming needs an explicit print exemption and a real installed-iPad check.** A fixed overlay can otherwise darken printed pages/PDFs; the repository already removes screen-only effects in print ([site.css:218](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/styles/site.css:218), [dock.css:1072](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/styles/dock.css:1072)). Add a print rule disabling the overlay and dialog filter. Also, the proposed Playwright run cannot answer the plan’s acknowledged iOS-standalone uncertainty: safe-area insets are zero on every development machine ([tokens.css:201](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/styles/tokens.css:201)). Require an installed-iPad pass covering first paint, portrait/landscape, elastic overscroll seams, status-bar/home-indicator edges, and an open dialog.
+
+## P2
+
+- **The px-font guard is narrower than its stated guarantee.** A stylesheet-only scan misses Tailwind arbitrary sizes and inline/SVG sizes, including [AddArticle.tsx:331](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/AddArticle.tsx:331), [DataTable.tsx:546](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/lib/DataTable.tsx:546), and [SketchView.tsx:110](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/SketchView.tsx:110). Either scan TS/TSX with a reasoned allowlist or narrow the claim to CSS. Add 18px and 22px to the existing layout and rotation sweeps, which currently stop at 20px ([layout.test.ts:186](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/tests/layout.test.ts:186), [reader-after-a-rotation-in-a-browser.test.ts:121](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/tests/reader-after-a-rotation-in-a-browser.test.ts:121)).
+
+- **The modal inventory is incomplete.** Sketch ([SketchView.tsx:553](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/SketchView.tsx:553)) and Command Bar ([CommandBar.tsx:2235](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/CommandBar.tsx:2235)) also use `showModal()`. The generic selector covers them, but test at least the full-viewport Command Bar. The `::backdrop` filter is unnecessary and relies on custom-property inheritance that existing styles deliberately avoid ([lightbox.css:62](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/styles/lightbox.css:62)); filter the dialog itself and leave its already-dark backdrop alone.
+
+- **`/design` is not prior proof and conflicts with the new setting.** Its comment calls the 20px root a diagnostic for mixed-unit failures ([DesignPage.tsx:616](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/DesignPage.tsx:616)). It writes an inline `20px`, overriding `data-text-size`; under “Largest,” enabling it would shrink the page ([DesignPage.tsx:635](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/DesignPage.tsx:635)). Define it as an explicit override, disable it under a saved non-default size, or replace it with a computed-root display.
+
+- **Support/documentation steps should be explicit.** Add both comfort values to feedback diagnostics, which currently record only Appearance and resolved theme ([feedback-diagnostics.ts:179](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/feedback-diagnostics.ts:179)). Make the Help update unconditional and regenerate the committed corpus ([help-page.md:112](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/docs/project/help-page.md:112)). The runtime module should also copy Appearance’s `pageshow`/bfcache and failed-write behavior, not merely its storage listener ([appearance.ts:113](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/appearance.ts:113)).
+
+Per-device `localStorage` is the right choice for this version: both values must exist before first paint, brightness is plainly device/environment-specific, and server synchronization would still need a local cache and conflict policy. Signed-out/static pages already preserve the boot script because page generation replaces only the managed head region ([build-site-pages.ts:82](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/scripts/build-site-pages.ts:82), [page-head.ts:253](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/public/page-head.ts:253)).
+
+The overlay’s `pointer-events:none` is safe for the existing `elementFromPoint` navigation ([keynav.ts:695](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/keynav.ts:695)). Spine and sticky offsets measure actual DOM geometry rather than assuming 16px ([Spine.tsx:188](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/Spine.tsx:188), [scroll.ts:179](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbq645m0-dim-mode-and-text-size/src/web/scroll.ts:179)); I found no virtualised row-height constant that needs conversion.
+
+**BUILD WITH CHANGES**
